						<p>In this series, we have explored several ways to incorporate R cod=
e into SAS programs and create R scripts within SAS using PROC R. In this p=
ost, we'll take that integration a step further by using the <strong>R Prog=
ram</strong> step in SAS Data and AI Studio flows. Flows provide a visual w=
ay to combine SAS data preparation and processing with R programming, allow=
ing you to take advantage of the strengths of both languages within a singl=
e workflow.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> This post is based on the 2026.06 stable release =
of SAS Viya.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h2 id=3D"toc-hId-1853365411">SAS Studio Flows</h2>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>If you are asking yourself, =E2=80=9CWhat is a =E2=80=98flow=E2=80=99?=
=E2=80=9D, SAS Data and AI Studio Flows offer a low-code option for analyzi=
ng data with SAS Viya. A <em>flow</em> is a sequence of operations on data.=
 Data and operations are represented in SAS Data and AI Studio by steps tha=
t you can access from the <strong>Steps</strong> section of the navigation =
pane. Each step in a flow is represented by a node on the flow canvas. Whil=
e SAS provides several predefined steps to use in flows, users and develope=
rs also build custom steps to perform specific tasks. The<strong> R Program=
</strong> step is a predefined step provided by SAS; however, users can als=
o use R code to create their own custom steps.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"text-align: center; color: #666; font-size: 80%;"><em><span cla=
ss=3D"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-center" image-alt=3D=
"exampleflow1.png" style=3D"width: 999px;"><span class=3D"lia-message-image=
-wrapper"><img src=3D"https://communities.sas.com/t5/image/serverpage/image=
-id/117468i45BDA35373DBFF3F/image-size/large?v=3Dv2&amp;px=3D999" role=3D"b=
utton" title=3D"exampleflow1.png" alt=3D"exampleflow1.png" li-image-url=3D"=
https://communities.sas.com/t5/image/serverpage/image-id/117468i45BDA35373D=
BFF3F?v=3Dv2" li-image-display-id=3D"'117468i45BDA35373DBFF3F'" li-message-=
uid=3D"'992995'" li-messages-message-image=3D"true" li-bindable=3D"" class=
=3D"lia-media-image" tabindex=3D"0" li-bypass-lightbox-when-linked=3D"true"=
 li-use-hover-links=3D"false" li-compiled=3D"true"><!----></span></span></e=
m></p>
<p style=3D"text-align: center; color: #666; font-size: 80%;"><em>Select an=
y image to see a larger version.</em><br><em>Mobile users: To view the imag=
es, select the "Full" version at the bottom of the page.</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Additional resources regarding SAS Studio Flows:</p>
<p><a href=3D"https://video.sas.com/detail/video/6325462242112/build-flows-=
with-sas-studio" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener nofollow noreferrer">Qui=
ck Start Video</a></p>
<p><a href=3D"https://go.documentation.sas.com/doc/en/webeditorflows/latest=
/titlepage.htm" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener nofollow noreferrer">Docu=
mentation</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h2 id=3D"toc-hId--698791550">Running the R Program Step</h2>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>To add the R Program step to a flow, click the <strong>Steps</strong> ic=
on in the lefthand pane. From the<strong> SAS Steps</strong> tab, expand th=
e <strong>Develop</strong> folder and either click and drag the <strong>R P=
rogram</strong> step to the flow or right-click the step and select <strong=
>Add to flow</strong>.</p>
